  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "HbZIWFFJwtBtmVnx3Pkmfjzag2I=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:00.447Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The session framed two revenue modes as an explicit trade rather than a sequence to be rushed. Consultancy projects are \"high-value\" but \"not scalable in the long term\". Product revenue is \"low-value\" but \"scalable in the long term\".\n\nThe connecting move is that PMF is established *along the way* \u2014 the consultancy work is not merely a bridge that funds the company until the product is ready, it is the mechanism by which the product learns what to be. That reframes each engagement as evidence-gathering with a paying client attached, and it sets a standard for which engagements are worth taking: one that generates revenue but no product learning is a worse deal than its invoice suggests.\n\nThe implied risk, not discussed in the session, is that consultancy revenue is comfortable enough to defer the transition indefinitely.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:00.447821Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:00.447826Z"
    }
  },
